# The hook scripts are bash, and Git for Windows converts text to CRLF on
# checkout by default, which breaks a bash script at its first command. `-text`
# turns line-ending conversion off for these files, so every checkout gets the
# LF bytes they were committed with. run-hook.cmd is a batch/bash polyglot; its
# batch half never jumps to a label (no goto, no call), so cmd.exe reads it
# correctly with LF too.
#
# This replaced a repo-wide `* text=auto eol=lf`. Anthropic's plugin directory
# stops validating a repository whose .gitattributes carries attributes that
# rewrite file contents, and an eol rule was too close to that to risk. `-text`
# asks git to leave contents alone, and it is scoped to the files that break.
hooks/session-start -text
hooks/user-prompt-submit -text
hooks/run-hook.cmd -text
.githooks/* -text
